+/* ---------- v1.6.6b overflow fixes (bugs C + D) ---------- */
+/* BUG C: WAN-page "DNS List" flyout (#dns_list_Block.clientlist_viewlist) inherits
+   the stock device-map.css rule (position:absolute; margin-top:-920px; height:auto;
+   overflow:auto) tuned for the short device-map list. The tall six-category WAN DNS
+   list grows past the viewport and height:auto defeats its own overflow, so the lower
+   rows are clipped/unreachable. Re-anchor it to the viewport with a real inner scroll. */
+#dns_list_Block.clientlist_viewlist{
+  position:fixed!important;
+  top:50%!important;left:50%!important;
+  margin-top:0!important;margin-left:0!important;
+  transform:translate(-50%,-50%)!important;
+  max-height:88vh!important;overflow-y:auto!important}
+/* static-DHCP client picker (LAN > DHCP Server, owner-directed v1.7.4). The
+   Manually-Assigned-IP dropdown (#ClientList_Block_PC) inherits .clientlist_dropdown
+   (device-map.css:990): position:absolute + height:auto + overflow-y:auto - height:auto
+   defeats its own overflow, and the shell frame auto-sizes to BODY height only, so a
+   DOWNWARD list grows past the frame and clips. The first fix escaped the clip by
+   centering it in the viewport (position:fixed), which detached it far from the button
+   (owner-reported on v1.7.3 metal). FIX: anchor it to its own input cell and open it
+   UPWARD - the list then overlays the already-rendered DHCP config above the input, so
+   the frame never has to grow (no clip) and it sits right on the pull-arrow. Capped
+   height + inner scroll for long client lists. Scoped via :has() to this page's unique
+   static-lease MAC input; ~20 other pages share the id and keep their stock anchoring. */
+body:has(input[name="dhcp_staticmac_x_0"]) td:has(> input[name="dhcp_staticmac_x_0"]){
+  position:relative!important}
+body:has(input[name="dhcp_staticmac_x_0"]) #ClientList_Block_PC.clientlist_dropdown{
+  position:absolute!important;
+  top:auto!important;
+  bottom:100%!important;          /* open upward, directly above the input/button */
+  left:0!important;
+  margin:0 0 4px 0!important;
+  max-height:260px!important;
+  overflow-y:auto!important;
+  z-index:1000!important}
+/* BUG D: Network Map status iframe (#statusframe) is pinned to 760px but the inner
+   clients.asp document (client rows + tall NM min-heights) is taller and has no inner
+   scroll region, so the iframe's own scrollbar stacks against the page scrollbar = a
+   persistent double/stray bar. Give the client list its own scroll so the iframe stops
+   overflowing (reaper_content.css is loaded inside the statusframe document). */
+#client_list_Block{max-height:600px!important;overflow-y:auto!important;overflow-x:hidden!important}
